KZ2 patch 6060 (ENHANCEMENT): keyboard tilt keys for the valves and demolition charges (Discord
tester on 0.1.7: "breach charge still won't work, requires controller tilt").

Without a motion sensor the valves and charges take the tilt from the right stick X (patch 6049 + the title port's
motion hook) while the game's grab (GrabLeftHand/GrabRightHand, L1 + R1, which no pad layout moves) is held. With a
keyboard that took four keys at once: the two grab keys (F and Mouse1 under the Standard layouts; under Modern the
keys follow their Standard action on foot, patch 6050, so L1 came from Mouse2) plus J or L for the stick, and nothing
told a player so. Now:
- keybinds.ini inputs tilt_left / tilt_right (defaults Z / X; file only, the Keyboard page keeps its 24 rows):
  stick-direction bits 8 / 9 (PadKbState.dirs is 16 bits now).
- pad_kb_tilt (pure): a held tilt key gives the grab (L1 + R1, raw, after 6050's roles) and the right stick X at
  0 / 255, only while a valve or charge controller reads the tilt; both held, the one pressed last wins (roll from one
  to the other without letting go of the grab, as a charge's two arm windows want).
- cellPad.c: pad_motion_tilt_note() (called by the motion hook each time it feeds a valve or charge controller), the
  keys act within 300 ms of the last note, so outside those they never fire or melee; one "[keys] tilt left/right/off"
  line per change.
Host test tools/runtime/test_kb_tilt.sh; tools/runtime/test_kb_rows.py allows the two file-only inputs.

